{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q408215","formula":"C₂ClF₃","hill":"C2ClF3","elements":["C","F","Cl"],"composition":{"C":2.0,"F":3.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Chlorotrifluoroethene","ru":"1,1,2-Трифтор-2-хлорэтилен"},"descriptions":{"en":"Chlorotrifluoroethylene (CTFE) is a chlorofluorocarbon with chemical formula CFCl=CF2. It is commonly used as a refrigerant in cryogenic applications. CTFE has a carbon-carbon double bond and so can be polymerized to form polychlorotrifluoroethylene or copolymerized to produce the plastic ECTFE. PCTFE has the trade name Neoflon PCTFE from Daikin Industries in Japan, and it used to be produced under the trade name Kel-F from 3M Corporation in Minnesota.","ru":"1,1,2-Трифтор-2-хлорэтилен — относится к фторолефинам — алкенам, в которых один или несколько атомов водорода замещены атомами фтора. Является непредельным фторорганическим соединением и служит в качестве мономера (Мономер-3) для производства фторкаучука СКФ-32 — сополимера с Мономером-2."},"fame":19,"pubchemCid":6594,"mass":116.47,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(=C(F)Cl)(F)F","inchikey":"UUAGAQFQZIEFAH-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-chloro-1,2,2-trifluoroethene","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"6594","atoms":6,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.855,"y":0.971,"z":0.0,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-0.929,"y":-1.516,"z":0.0,"el":"F"},{"x":1.06,"y":1.436,"z":0.0,"el":"F"},{"x":1.635,"y":-0.824,"z":0.0,"el":"F"},{"x":-0.6,"y":-0.206,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.689,"y":0.138,"z":0.0,"el":"C"}],"bonds":[[0,4,1],[1,4,1],[2,5,1],[3,5,1],[4,5,2]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q408215","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chlorotrifluoroethylene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"desc